function cowspec(s:seq<nat>, u:seq<nat>): nat
requires 0 <= |u| == |s| && nomultiples(u)
{recccow(s, u, 0)}
{"spec_element": "requires",
 "proof_obligation": "initiation",
 "diagnosis": "cowspec's precondition only requires nomultiples(u). Its body calls recccow(s, u, 0), which requires 0 <= i <= |s| == |u|. Nothing in cowspec's precondition gives |s| == |u|, so the callee's precondition cannot be proved (counterexample |s|=1, |u|=2). The fix is to strengthen cowspec's requires with |u| == |s|, as bullspec already does. All callers (BullsCows, TEST) supply sequences of equal length."}

